diagnosis_text:
No connectivity fault is present on the Location B access segment. PC15 (172.18.51.15) and PC16 (172.18.51.16) are Layer-2 adjacent on switch10 and communicate normally. From PC15 to PC16, ICMP echo succeeded with 0% loss and ~0.52–0.69 ms RTT; from PC16 to PC15, ICMP echo also succeeded with 0% loss and ~0.41–0.44 ms RTT. Both hosts have correct /24 addressing and a direct connected route to 172.18.51.0/24. ARP/neighbour entries for each other are present on both hosts, confirming L2 resolution.

On the access switch, the exact ports serving these hosts are healthy: switch10 eth1 (to PC15) and eth2 (to PC16) are UP, link detected, 10G Full-Duplex, and counters show RX/TX packets incrementing with zero errors or drops:
- eth1: RX 17, TX 23, errors 0, drops 0
- eth2: RX 25, TX 29, errors 0, drops 0

Mechanism wise, if frames were being dropped or a port were down, we would see ARP failures and/or ICMP loss; neither is observed. Localization confirms the access ports and host NICs are operational.

Root cause: No reproducible network-layer fault; the reported issue is not occurring at this time.

Corrective fix: None required on the network. If application connectivity still appears intermittent, investigate endpoint firewalls/app settings and capture timestamps for correlation; continue to monitor switch10 port error counters for any future anomalies. 
